{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HeckeMarkovTransition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HeckeMarkovTransition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.GroupWithZero.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.not_markov_chain_factorization_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.not_markov_chain_factorization_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L252-L269","doc":"**The former axiom `markov_chain_factorization_axiom` was false**\n(removed 2026-11-15, with its wrapper `markov_chain_factorization_exists`).\nIt quantified `totalTrace : ℝ` universally, so it asserted that every\nreal number equals the product of vertex volumes. The intended statement\nneeds `totalTrace` to be the Markov trace of the braid, which this file\ndoes not define; recorded as open in bean `qou-n2un`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.eigenvalue_expectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.eigenvalue_expectation","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L224-L239","doc":"The probability-weighted expectation of the crossing eigenvalues:\n\nE[eigenvalue] = p₊ · q + p₋ · (−q⁻¹) = q − q⁻¹\n\nThis is the spectral content of the Markov parameter:\nthe expected eigenvalue under the stochastic transition operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.step","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L222-L222","doc":"Hecke reduction at this generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.spectral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.spectral","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L220-L220","doc":"Spectral data (q parameter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CrossingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L218-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CrossingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CrossingData","kind":"structure","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L212-L222","doc":"A single crossing, fully described: spectral data + Hecke reduction.\n\nThe Hecke reduction a_i T_i + b_i evaluated through the spectral\nidempotents gives:\n  a_i · (q · e₊ − q⁻¹ · e₋) + b_i\nand the Markov trace picks out the expectation V̂_i = z a_i + b_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.trace_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.trace_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L203-L208","doc":"The product is nonzero when all vertex volumes are nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.totalTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.totalTrace","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L198-L201","doc":"The product of the vertex volumes, `∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.steps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.steps","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L196-L196","doc":"The transition steps, one per generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.n_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.n_ge","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L194-L194","doc":"At least two strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.n","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L192-L192","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L190-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovChainFactorization","kind":"structure","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L169-L196","doc":"**Product factorization from independence.**\n\nGiven n−1 independent transition steps, the total Markov trace\nis the product of vertex volumes:\n\n  tr_M(ρ(β)) = ∏_{i=0}^{n−2} V̂_i\n\nEach V̂_i depends only on the local crossing data (a_i, b_i),\nnot on the other generators.  This holds for words that use each\ngenerator once (one step per generator, as indexed by `Fin (n-1)`\nhere).  It fails when a generator repeats: tr_M(σ₁σ₂σ₁) = h z² + z,\nnot z³ (corrected 2026-11-16).  The product is a definition here\n(`MarkovChainFactorization.totalTrace`); its identification with\nthe Markov trace of the grouped word is not proved in this file.\n(Until 2026-11-16 `totalTrace` was a free field and the product\nformula a structure field, so the structure assumed the formula.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.vertexVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.vertexVolume","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L158-L165","doc":"The vertex volume = one-step conditional expectation:\nV̂_i = z · a_i + b_i.\n\nUnder the Markov trace, tr_M(a_i T_i + b_i) = z · a_i + b_i\nbecause tr_M(T_i) = z (Markov property) and tr_M(1) = 1\n(normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L156-L156","doc":"z ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.z","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L154-L154","doc":"Markov parameter z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.b","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L152-L152","doc":"Hecke reduction constant b_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.a","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Hecke reduction coefficient a_i (coefficient of T_i). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTransitionStep","kind":"structure","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L138-L156","doc":"The Markov chain transition data at a single crossing.\n\nThe Markov trace property tr_M(x T_n) = z · tr_M(x) says that\nthe expectation value of generator n is independent of the history\nx ∈ H_{n−1}(q).  The vertex volume V̂_i = z · a_i + b_i is the\none-step conditional expectation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.bias","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.bias","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L129-L134","doc":"p₊ = p₋ = 1/2 at q = 1 would give the classical fair walk.\nHere we record the identity: at any q, p₊ − p₋ = (q − q⁻¹)/(q + q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus_gt_p_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus_gt_p_minus","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L121-L127","doc":"p₊ > p₋ when q > 1 (the symmetric channel is favoured). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.boltzmann_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.boltzmann_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L106-L119","doc":"**Boltzmann ratio**: p₊/p₋ = q².\n\nThe ratio of transition probabilities equals q², the Boltzmann\nweight for a single crossing.  Note that `K_i = p₊·id + p₋·s_i` is\ndoubly stochastic (`s_i` is a permutation matrix), so its stationary law\nis the uniform measure, not the Mallows measure: q² here is a one-step\nratio, not the fugacity of a stationary distribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_minus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_minus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L100-L104","doc":"p₋ > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L94-L98","doc":"p₊ > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.prob_sum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.prob_sum_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**p₊ + p₋ = 1**: the transition probabilities form a probability\ndistribution.  This is the normalisation of eigenvalues to a\nstochastic operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_minus","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The antisymmetric (−q⁻¹-eigenvalue) transition probability:\np₋ = q⁻¹ / (q + q⁻¹) = 1 / (q² + 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.p_plus","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L74-L77","doc":"The symmetric (q-eigenvalue) transition probability:\np₊ = q / (q + q⁻¹) = q² / (q² + 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The spectral gap is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L59-L65","doc":"The spectral gap is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.gap","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The spectral gap q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L53-L53","doc":"q ≠ 1 (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L51-L51","doc":"q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.q","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Deformation parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SpectralIdempotentData","kind":"structure","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.lean#L36-L53","doc":"Spectral idempotent data for a single Hecke generator T_i.\n\nGiven the quadratic relation (T_i − q)(T_i + q⁻¹) = 0, the two\neigenvalues are λ₊ = q and λ₋ = −q⁻¹.  The spectral projectors are:\n\n  e₊ = (T_i + q⁻¹) / (q + q⁻¹)     (projects onto the q-eigenspace)\n  e₋ = (q − T_i) / (q + q⁻¹)        (projects onto the −q⁻¹-eigenspace)\n\nWe work at the level of eigenvalues (scalars), which suffices for\nthe transition probability computation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-markov-transition","label":"prop:hecke-markov-transition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-markov-transition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}